This plugin logs block creates and destroys to a MySQL database. It can be used as an anti-griefing tool to find out who made a particular edit, or even roll back changes by certain players.
Originally written by bootswithdefer for hMod ported to Bukkit by me, because of impossibleness to identfy griefers. Due to BigBrother also did't work, I was forced to do it myself. The honor belongs to bootswithdefer for the sourcecode, I only spended nearly 8 hours to transcribe. All functions except sign text logging shold work as in hMod. The use of permissions plugin is possible, but not necessary.

tested on Poseidon 1.1.8

Build (JDK 8 + Maven):
1. Put Poseidon server.jar into testsrv/ (testsrv/server.jar)
2. mvn package (runs the unit tests too)
The plugin jar is written to testsrv/plugins/LogBlock.jar.

No MySQL connector jar is needed: the driver is bundled in Poseidon's server.jar.
Chest access logging (logChestAccess) works without Spout, see docs/chest-access.md.
Rollback, redo and clearlog ask for confirmation with /lb yes, see docs/confirmations.md.
Permissions are set in config.yml: groups, a default group for every player, players added by nickname (/lb group add), see docs/permissions.md. No permissions plugin needed.
Upgrading to 1.27 from the old build (1.26, commit 70001ed): see docs/upgrading.md.
Tests: unit tests run with mvn package; end-to-end tests with bots on a real server: bash tests/chest-access/run.sh, bash tests/permissions/run.sh, bash tests/fresh-install/run.sh, see tests/README.md.